WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.267
-James!
-Adam Sandler!

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.267
It is great to see you, bud.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hi! Hey!

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:07.133
I love ya!
Nice to see you all!

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.534
-We love having you on the show.
Thank you so much

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.467
for being here, bud.
-I'm very excited.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.300
-I want to -- I want to
congratulate you

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.501
because a week ago...
-Yes.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.501
-...you received
the Mark Twain Prize.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.434
-Yes. Yeah.
Isn't that wonderful?

00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:20.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:23.868
-American Humor.
At the Kennedy Center.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.133
That is a big deal, bud.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.601
-Very good.
-And well deserved.

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.868
It was so awesome.
-Yes, I enjoyed it.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.033
-Yeah, you did?

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:31.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.534
-I grew up loving Mark Twain.

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.901
You read --
You read "Tom Sawyer," anybody?

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.200
-I read it twice.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.067
-Wow! Wow!
You liked it that much?

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:46.901
-I was like, "Something about
this guy's connecting with me."

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.901
-Yeah. No. Yeah,
It was a really great time.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.567
-It was a star-studded night.
-Yes.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.167
-Everybody was there.
I got a picture right here.

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:53.267
-Yeah.
-One of your buddies here.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.400
-Who's that?
-Chris Rock.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.767
-Oh, yes.
Young Chris Rock showing up.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.968
-Chris Rock was in the house.
-Yeah.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.467
Look at him! He looks good!
-He's unbelievable.

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.901
-He stays handsome.
-He's unbelie--

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.968
He is very, very handsome.
But everybody -- I mean --

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.167
-Yeah.
-Everybody was there.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.968
-A bunch of my -- A bunch
of comedian friends came.

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.801
The Mark Twain thing is --
You want to show another one?

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.167
-Yeah. I dug out --
Another --

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.434
-I do. You felt it?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.767
-I thought you'd be yearning --
yearning to move on.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:18.067
-Itchy trigger finger?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.000
You felt me going over there?
-Yeah.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.834
-No. I was gonna say.
I know Conan was there.

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.467
Judd Apatow was there.
Spade was funny.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.767
-Yes.
-But then this one --

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:26.968
I thought this was
kind of a cool one.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.367
-Yeah. One of my best friends
was there.

00:01:28.367 --> 00:01:29.901
-Yeah, yeah. Wolf Blitzer.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:33.667
-Wolf Blitzer and I, we went
to junior high school together.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:37.133
[ Laughs ] No. No. I met --
I met him that night, man.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.701
"The Blitz," I call him.
-The Blitz!

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:40.033
-Yeah.
-Yeah, he was --

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.334
-I was hanging out with a --

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.467
with a whole different
type of people.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:44.767
-Yeah.

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:48.834
The whole night was great
and entertaining. Do --

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:49.901
You're a very humble guy.

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.501
You don't like
anyone talking about you.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.968
-You don't want to sit there
and have people compliment you

00:01:53.968 --> 00:01:56.033
and say you're good
and be in the room.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.934
You like hearing that
when you're not in the room.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.100
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.267
-Like a friend calling you up
and saying,

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.467
"Hey, I was talking
to so-and-so.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.601
He said good things about you."

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:04.868
-Yeah.
-You don't want to be there

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.467
hearing, like, "You know
what I like about you?"

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:07.601
And then you're like, "Oh, boy."

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:09.834
-You know who crushed?
Your wife, Jackie.

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.834
-My wife went on and did
a speech about me, everybody.

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.467
-Yeah.
-And she did -- she --

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-She was amazing.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:17.167
-She did great.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:19.000
She talked for, I said,
four minutes,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.434
and then she screamed eight.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.100
-[ Laughs ]
That's not there. Yeah.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.968
But, you know, they had a very
funny video that they showed.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.634
Here's --
-No. What is this?

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.033
-This is good.
Now, this is Kenny Smith.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:30.634
Oh, he's complimentary in it?

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.534
-NBA legend.
"Inside the NBA" analyst.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.367
-He saying good things
about my game?

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.834
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:36.901
-Oh, he said amazing things.

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.400
-Oh, I just can't wait
to see it.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.901
-Oh, yeah, here's him
talking about your game.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.567
-Yay.
-He is only a passer

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:45.501
at this stage in his career
with bad costuming

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:47.601
and whatever that -- Is that --
That's not even a costume.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.934
Oh, he actually --
This is a real clip

00:02:49.934 --> 00:02:52.234
of him actually playing.
I thought this was a movie set.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.634
Who wears a polo
and long shorts?

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.234
Who plays basketball
with sunglasses on?

00:02:57.234 --> 00:02:58.467
Listen to this.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.567
If your dog
can steal the ball from you,

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.367
you're in the wrong sport,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.100
-That is ridiculous.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.200
-What is he talking about?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.901
-First of all,
I do love Kenny Smith,

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:13.100
and he -- they catch --
These are bad moments.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.033
I have such a great game.
It's insane, everybody.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.667
The dog got lucky.
It bit my ball.

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:21.400
[ Laughter ]
No, I don't --

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.901
I'm telling you.
I'm older now. I'm 56!

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.534
-What? No.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.634
-I'm old, man!
-No, you're always young.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.767
Forever young.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.400
-Well, alright.
I'll pretend I'm young.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.567
But, honestly, when
I'm on the court and it's --

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:36.467
I'm dribbling
and I see other guys on my team,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.234
I never take the shot
because I'm like,

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.601
"He's better than me.
He's better than me."

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:41.200
Just --
That's why I look to pass.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.901
Then whenever I go --
And somebody will say to me,

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.267
"Hey, start shooting more."

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:46.701
I'll be like,
"Yeah, he's right, he's right."

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.200
So then I take a shot and miss.
I go, "Didn't I tell you?"

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.701
-Yeah. Yeah.
You got to trust your gut.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.000
-Did you say I got a gut?
You son of a bitch!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.701
-No!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:59.200
-Son of a bitch, Jimmy?

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.667
-"Why, why, why?!"
-Why would you --

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.734
-"Why would you do that to me?"

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:04.868
"Adam Sandler Live,"
your standup tour.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.534
-Yes.
-By the way, you know,

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:08.334
I follow you on the socials
and Instagram.

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.834
It is the most amazing,
most fun thing.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:13.133
And even to look the next day
on your socials

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.734
and you go, "What happened?"

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.634
You have, like, famous friends
just drop in.

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:19.267
-My friends do come.
All my -- All my buddies

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.367
from growing up as a comedian.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:23.100
-Rob Schneider's very funny.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.567
-"Schneid Man"
comes all the time.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.434
-Chris Rock showed up.
-Kevin James.

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:28.801
-Kevin James. It was just --
-Nealon. Bobcat Gold--

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.400
All these guys come,
and they're really fun shows,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.834
and the crowds are really nice.

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.534
I'm playing in Philly,
by the way, guys!

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:36.567
I'm playing in Philly.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.100
That's gonna be great.
-But you --

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.567
You started doing
these theaters,

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:40.968
and then
now you're doing arenas.

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:42.667
-I know, I know.
It's phenomenal.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:45.067
We're having the best time.
The crowds are having fun.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.701
We -- I tell jokes.
I play tunes.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:51.200
And it's really -- it's been
a whole new part of my life.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.901
It's fun.
-More with Adam Sandler

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.300
when we come back.
Stick around, everybody!

